  "prompt": "The function f is defined by f(x)=x2+10x+24. If g(x)=f(x−2) and h(x)=g(x)−f(x), what is the value of h(0)?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "−25",
    "B": "−16",
    "C": "−1",
    "D": "1"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "B",
  "explanation": "First, find $g(x) = f(x-2) = (x-2)^2 + 10(x-2) + 24$. Expanding gives $g(x) = x^2 - 4x + 4 + 10x - 20 + 24 = x^2 + 6x + 8$. Then $h(x) = g(x) - f(x) = (x^2 + 6x + 8) - (x^2 + 10x + 24) = -4x - 16$. Therefore, $h(0) = -4(0) - 16 = -16$.",
